#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1
msgid "Embewi — Contrat Core ↔ Agent (v2)"
msgstr "Embewi — Core ↔ Agent Contract (v2)"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:3
msgid ""
"Spec de référence figée. Toute implémentation (Runtime Core en Go, Agent "
"en ESP-IDF/C) doit s'y conformer. Les sections marquées **[NORMATIF]** "
"sont des contraintes ; les sections **[RÉSERVE]** sont hors MVP et "
"documentées pour ne pas recoder l'API plus tard."
msgstr ""
"Frozen reference spec. Every implementation (Core runtime in Go, Agent "
"in ESP-IDF/C) must conform to it. Sections marked **[NORMATIVE]** are "
"binding constraints; sections marked **[RESERVED]** are out of MVP scope"
" and documented so the API doesn't need to be recoded later."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:8
msgid ""
"Version protocole : `v1alpha1` Préfixe des endpoints inbound : "
"`/v1alpha1/...` (versionner dès le départ — les devices sur le terrain "
"survivront à plusieurs versions de Core)."
msgstr ""
"Protocol version: `v1alpha1` Inbound endpoint prefix: `/v1alpha1/...` "
"(versioned from day one — devices in the field will outlive several "
"Core versions)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:14
msgid "0. Périmètre et hypothèses réseau **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "0. Scope and network assumptions **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:23
msgid "Conséquence de l'asymétrie :"
msgstr "Consequence of this asymmetry:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:30
msgid ""
"Le jour où un device n'est plus joignable en inbound (NAT), le mode PUSH "
"s'effondre : c'est une bifurcation d'architecture (mode PULL), pas un "
"correctif. Elle est nommée ici, pas découverte en phase 4."
msgstr ""
"The day a device is no longer reachable inbound (NAT), PUSH mode "
"collapses: that's an architectural fork (PULL mode), not a patch. It's "
"named here up front, not discovered in phase 4."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:36
msgid "1. Modèle de sécurité **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "1. Security model **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:38
msgid "Principe directeur :"
msgstr "Guiding principle:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:45
msgid ""
"La vérification de signature n'est **pas** « Core OU ESP ». C'est **les "
"deux**, avec autorité finale au bootloader — le seul composant qui ne "
"peut pas mentir."
msgstr ""
"Signature verification is **not** \"Core OR ESP\". It's **both**, with "
"final authority resting with the bootloader — the only component that "
"cannot lie."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Couche"
msgstr "Layer"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Rôle de sécurité"
msgstr "Security role"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Qui porte la confiance"
msgstr "Who holds the trust"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Core"
msgstr "Core"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Pull OCI/ORAS, vérifie digest + signature + compat avant de transférer"
msgstr "Pulls OCI/ORAS, verifies digest + signature + compat before transferring"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Efficacité (pas confiance)"
msgstr "Efficiency (not trust)"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Transport"
msgstr "Transport"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Endpoint OTA authentifié (mTLS, ou token par node au minimum)"
msgstr "Authenticated OTA endpoint (mTLS, or at minimum a per-node token)"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Empêche l'inbound anonyme"
msgstr "Blocks anonymous inbound"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "ESP — réception"
msgstr "ESP — reception"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "N'accepte un OTA que d'un Core autorisé (auth transport)"
msgstr "Only accepts an OTA from an authorized Core (transport auth)"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Filtre l'appelant"
msgstr "Filters the caller"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Bootloader"
msgstr "Bootloader"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "**Secure Boot v2** : refuse de booter toute image non/ mal signée"
msgstr "**Secure Boot v2**: refuses to boot any un/mis-signed image"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "**Racine de confiance**"
msgstr "**Root of trust**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "eFuse"
msgstr "eFuse"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "**Anti-rollback** : bloque le downgrade vers image signée plus ancienne"
msgstr "**Anti-rollback**: blocks downgrade to an older signed image"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Matériel, irréversible"
msgstr "Hardware, irreversible"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Flash"
msgstr "Flash"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "**Flash encryption** : si vol physique du device plausible"
msgstr "**Flash encryption**: if physical device theft is plausible"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Confidentialité at-rest"
msgstr "At-rest confidentiality"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Runtime"
msgstr "Runtime"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Rollback validé **localement** après self-check (cf. §3)"
msgstr "Rollback validated **locally** after self-check (see §3)"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md
msgid "Intégrité fonctionnelle"
msgstr "Functional integrity"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:58
msgid ""
"Pourquoi le Core ne peut pas être racine de confiance : un ESP qui reçoit"
" des octets sur `/ota/write` n'a aucun moyen cryptographique de savoir "
"que ces octets sont ceux que le Core a vérifiés. Sans Secure Boot, "
"quiconque atteint l'IP de management peut écrire une image arbitraire. "
"**Sans auth inbound, `/ota/activate` est une primitive de reboot offerte "
"au premier venu sur le LAN.**"
msgstr ""
"Why the Core cannot be the root of trust: an ESP receiving bytes on "
"`/ota/write` has no cryptographic way of knowing that these bytes are "
"the ones the Core verified. Without Secure Boot, anyone who reaches the "
"management IP can write an arbitrary image. **Without inbound auth, "
"`/ota/activate` is a reboot primitive handed to the first comer on the "
"LAN.**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:64
msgid "Transport — décision MVP explicite :"
msgstr "Transport — explicit MVP decision:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:71
msgid ""
"Justification : mTLS sur ESP-IDF est faisable, mais entraîne "
"immédiatement gestion de CA, distribution + rotation de certificats, "
"horloge fiable (validation de validité) et empreinte mémoire. Pour un "
"premier prototype, HTTPS + token par node + Secure Boot v2 est un socle "
"cohérent et défendable. mTLS est la cible, pas le point de départ."
msgstr ""
"Rationale: mTLS on ESP-IDF is feasible, but immediately drags in CA "
"management, certificate distribution + rotation, a reliable clock "
"(validity checking), and memory footprint. For a first prototype, "
"HTTPS + per-node token + Secure Boot v2 is a coherent, defensible "
"baseline. mTLS is the target, not the starting point."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:77
msgid "Exigences minimales MVP :"
msgstr "Minimal MVP requirements:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:78
msgid ""
"`CONFIG_SECURE_BOOT_V2_ENABLED` — sinon le projet n'est pas défendable en"
" revue sécu."
msgstr ""
"`CONFIG_SECURE_BOOT_V2_ENABLED` — otherwise the project is not "
"defensible in a security review."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:79
msgid ""
"Auth sur tous les endpoints inbound : **token par node sur HTTPS** (cible"
" mTLS)."
msgstr ""
"Auth on all inbound endpoints: **per-node token over HTTPS** (mTLS is "
"the target)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:80
msgid ""
"Anti-rollback eFuse activé dès qu'un schéma de version de sécurité est en"
" place."
msgstr ""
"eFuse anti-rollback enabled as soon as a security version scheme is in "
"place."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:81
msgid "Flash encryption : optionnel MVP, obligatoire si le device peut être volé."
msgstr "Flash encryption: optional for MVP, mandatory if the device can be stolen."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:83
msgid "Défense en profondeur réseau (opt-in production, §8) :"
msgstr "Network defense in depth (production opt-in, §8):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:84
msgid ""
"VLAN dédié : subnet ESP isolé, seuls les nodes Core ont une route L3 vers"
" lui."
msgstr ""
"Dedicated VLAN: isolated ESP subnet, only Core nodes have an L3 route "
"to it."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:85
msgid ""
"NetworkPolicy K8s : egress vers le subnet ESP réservé aux Pods Core "
"(ipBlock)."
msgstr ""
"K8s NetworkPolicy: egress to the ESP subnet restricted to Core Pods "
"(ipBlock)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:86
msgid ""
"`CONFIG_EMBEWI_ENABLE_IP_FILTER` : l'agent rejette les connexions hors "
"CIDR autorisé avant tout handler (`open_fn` httpd). CIDR configurable via"
" McuConfigMap `allowed_cidr` — utiliser le CIDR du cluster plutôt que "
"l'IP exacte du Pod Core."
msgstr ""
"`CONFIG_EMBEWI_ENABLE_IP_FILTER`: the agent rejects connections outside "
"the allowed CIDR before any handler runs (httpd `open_fn`). CIDR "
"configurable via the McuConfigMap `allowed_cidr` key — use the cluster "
"CIDR rather than the Core Pod's exact IP."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:90
msgid ""
"**Rayon d'action d'un token compromis (NORMATIF).** Le token par node "
"n'autorise pas seulement les appels inbound sur son device. Via "
"`heartbeat.ip`, il pilote aussi `EndpointSlice.endpoints[].addresses` "
"(§8) — un attaquant en possession d'un token peut donc émettre un "
"heartbeat déclarant une `ip` arbitraire et détourner tout le trafic du "
"`Service` vers un endpoint qu'il contrôle, **sans jamais toucher au "
"device physique** (qui continue en parallèle d'émettre ses propres "
"heartbeats — un battement d'adresse plutôt qu'un état franc). Cohérent "
"avec le modèle `token == identité`, mais le rayon d'action réel dépasse «"
" appeler les endpoints inbound de ce device » : il inclut les "
"**consommateurs** du workload routé par ce `Service`. Détection côté "
"Core, cf. §8."
msgstr ""
"**Blast radius of a compromised token (NORMATIVE).** A per-node token "
"doesn't only authorize inbound calls on its device. Via `heartbeat.ip`, "
"it also drives `EndpointSlice.endpoints[].addresses` (§8) — an attacker "
"holding a token can therefore send a heartbeat claiming an arbitrary "
"`ip` and hijack all of the `Service`'s traffic toward an endpoint they "
"control, **without ever touching the physical device** (which keeps "
"emitting its own heartbeats in parallel — an address flutter rather "
"than a clean-cut state). Consistent with the `token == identity` model,"
" but the real blast radius goes beyond \"calling this device's inbound "
"endpoints\": it includes the **consumers** of the workload routed by "
"that `Service`. Detected Core-side, see §8."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:102
msgid ""
"**Dev vs Prod.** Ces exigences sont des opérations eFuse "
"**irréversibles** : elles ne s'activent **pas en dev**. Elles sont "
"portées par un profil de build séparé et opt-in "
"(`sdkconfig.defaults.prod` + `CONFIG_EMBEWI_VERIFY_CORE_CERT` pour l'auth"
" des flux sortants). Procédure complète, gestion de la clé de signature "
"et de la CA du Core : **`embewi-prod-security.md`**. Le flux de dev reste"
" chiffré-mais-non-authentifié et librement reflashable."
msgstr ""
"**Dev vs Prod.** These requirements are **irreversible** eFuse "
"operations: they are **not** enabled in dev. They are carried by a "
"separate, opt-in build profile (`sdkconfig.defaults.prod` + "
"`CONFIG_EMBEWI_VERIFY_CORE_CERT` for outbound auth). Full procedure, "
"signing key and Core CA management: **`embewi-prod-security.md`**. The "
"dev flow stays encrypted-but-unauthenticated and freely reflashable."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:111
msgid "1a. Enrôlement et identité du device **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "1a. Device enrollment and identity **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:113
msgid ""
"Un device n'est pas « ajouté » par le Core : il **se présente**. "
"L'identité et le secret d'authentification sont établis **hors-bande au "
"provisioning**, pas négociés en ligne (pas d'AC, pas de CSR en MVP — cf. "
"§1)."
msgstr ""
"A device is not \"added\" by the Core: it **introduces itself**. "
"Identity and the authentication secret are established **out-of-band "
"at provisioning**, not negotiated online (no CA, no CSR in the MVP — "
"see §1)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:125
msgid ""
"**Durcissement du provisioning (l'AP est le moment le plus faible — aucun"
" secret partagé n'existe encore) :**"
msgstr ""
"**Provisioning hardening (the AP is the weakest moment — no shared "
"secret exists yet):**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:141
msgid ""
"Le couple `(node_id, token)` est l'identité du device. Le token est le "
"secret partagé : l'admin le recopie dans le Core (typiquement un "
"`McuSecret`) au moment où il crée le `McuNode` correspondant. **Le Core "
"et le device connaissent le token ; le réseau ne le voit jamais en clair "
"(HTTPS, §1).**"
msgstr ""
"The `(node_id, token)` pair is the device's identity. The token is the "
"shared secret: the admin copies it into the Core (typically a "
"`McuSecret`) when creating the matching `McuNode`. **The Core and the "
"device know the token; the network never sees it in the clear (HTTPS, "
"§1).**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:146
msgid "Découverte côté Core — deux modèles compatibles :"
msgstr "Core-side discovery — two compatible models:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:159
msgid "Invariants côté agent (ce que ce repo garantit) :"
msgstr "Agent-side invariants (what this repo guarantees):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:169
msgid ""
"Le Core est responsable de refuser un `node_id` en double (cf. §7, "
"`AmbiguousBinding`) — l'agent ne déduplique pas, il s'annonce."
msgstr ""
"The Core is responsible for rejecting a duplicate `node_id` (see §7, "
"`AmbiguousBinding`) — the agent does not deduplicate, it just announces"
" itself."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:174
msgid "2. États de l'agent **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "2. Agent states **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:185
msgid "Transitions clés :"
msgstr "Key transitions:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:198
msgid ""
"Règle d'or côté heartbeat : **un device en `pending_verify` continue "
"d'émettre un heartbeat** portant `state: \"pending_verify\"`. Pas de "
"silence pendant la fenêtre de validation (le silence est indistinguable "
"d'un crash)."
msgstr ""
"Golden rule on the heartbeat side: **a device in `pending_verify` keeps "
"emitting a heartbeat** carrying `state: \"pending_verify\"`. No silence "
"during the validation window (silence is indistinguishable from a "
"crash)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:204
msgid "3. Séquence OTA critique **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "3. Critical OTA sequence **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:206
msgid ""
"C'est le cœur dur du projet — le bout qui peut l'invalider. Le rollback "
"réel n'est **pas** piloté par le Core : c'est le bootloader ESP-IDF qui "
"le fait."
msgstr ""
"This is the hard core of the project — the part that can invalidate it."
" The actual rollback is **not** driven by the Core: the ESP-IDF "
"bootloader does it."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:224
msgid "Deux garde-fous **obligatoires**, l'un local, l'autre côté Core :"
msgstr "Two **mandatory** safeguards, one local, the other Core-side:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:239
msgid ""
"Le signal de santé sert **deux maîtres** : il valide l'image localement "
"(`mark_valid`) ET il ouvre le routage côté cluster (EndpointSlice ready)."
" Si on rate ça, on obtient des ESP qui annoncent « ready » sur une image "
"qui se fera revert au prochain reset."
msgstr ""
"The health signal serves **two masters**: it validates the image "
"locally (`mark_valid`) AND it opens up routing cluster-side "
"(EndpointSlice ready). Get this wrong and you end up with ESPs "
"announcing \"ready\" on an image that will revert on the next reset."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:244
msgid ""
"Confirmation de fin de déploiement émise par l'agent (cf. §5, ré-écho du "
"`deployment_id` — pas seulement le digest, car deux déploiements peuvent "
"partager un digest) :"
msgstr ""
"Deployment-completion confirmation emitted by the agent (see §5, "
"echoing back `deployment_id` — not just the digest, since two "
"deployments can share a digest):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:259
msgid "4. Endpoints inbound (Core → ESP) **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "4. Inbound endpoints (Core → ESP) **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:261
msgid "`GET /v1alpha1/info`"
msgstr "`GET /v1alpha1/info`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:263
msgid "Identité matérielle **+ slot stagé** (clé de l'idempotence, cf. §6)."
msgstr "Hardware identity **+ staged slot** (the key to idempotence, see §6)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:292
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`staged.state` ∈ `none | written | activating`. Quand aucun slot n'est "
"stagé : `\"staged\": { \"state\": \"none\" }`."
msgstr ""
"`staged.state` ∈ `none | written | activating`. When no slot is staged: "
"`\"staged\": { \"state\": \"none\" }`."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:295
msgid ""
"**Découverte de version d'API (NORMATIF).** `api_versions` liste les "
"versions de protocole `/v1alpha1`-style supportées par l'agent, la plus "
"élevée en premier. Règles :"
msgstr ""
"**API version discovery (NORMATIVE).** `api_versions` lists the "
"`/v1alpha1`-style protocol versions supported by the agent, highest "
"first. Rules:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:309
msgid "`GET /v1alpha1/health`"
msgstr "`GET /v1alpha1/health`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:311
msgid "Health **local**, pas seulement réseau."
msgstr "**Local** health, not just network reachability."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:321
msgid "`status` ∈ `ok | degraded | fail`."
msgstr "`status` ∈ `ok | degraded | fail`."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:323
msgid "`POST /v1alpha1/ota/prepare`"
msgstr "`POST /v1alpha1/ota/prepare`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:325
msgid ""
"Le Core annonce le firmware avant transfert. L'ESP vérifie la compat "
"**avant** tout octet (un binaire `esp32-s3` flashé sur `esp32` ne boote "
"pas)."
msgstr ""
"The Core announces the firmware before transfer. The ESP checks "
"compatibility **before** a single byte is sent (an `esp32-s3` binary "
"flashed onto an `esp32` won't boot)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:340
msgid "Réponse (accept) :"
msgstr "Response (accept):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:346
msgid ""
"Réponse (refus) — `reason` ∈ `chip_mismatch | layout_mismatch | "
"idf_incompatible | busy | size_too_large` :"
msgstr ""
"Response (rejection) — `reason` ∈ `chip_mismatch | layout_mismatch | "
"idf_incompatible | busy | size_too_large`:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:352
msgid "`PUT /v1alpha1/ota/write`"
msgstr "`PUT /v1alpha1/ota/write`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:354
msgid "Le Core streame le `.bin` brut. L'ESP ne connaît jamais OCI/ORAS."
msgstr "The Core streams the raw `.bin`. The ESP never knows about OCI/ORAS."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:356
msgid "Headers :"
msgstr "Headers:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:365 ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:477
#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:508 ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:529
#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:549
msgid "Réponse :"
msgstr "Response:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:371
msgid ""
"L'ESP calcule le digest **en incrémental, au fil de l'écriture** (SHA-256"
" streaming sur chaque chunk reçu via `esp_ota_write`), et compare au "
"header en fin de transfert. Pas de relecture de la partition flash après "
"coup. Rejet si mismatch (`status: \"digest_mismatch\"`). Le Core a "
"vérifié pour l'efficacité ; l'ESP revérifie ce qu'il a réellement écrit, "
"sans coût de relecture."
msgstr ""
"The ESP computes the digest **incrementally, as it writes** (streaming "
"SHA-256 on each chunk received via `esp_ota_write`), and compares it to "
"the header at the end of the transfer. No re-reading of the flash "
"partition afterward. Rejected on mismatch (`status: "
"\"digest_mismatch\"`). The Core verified for efficiency; the ESP "
"re-verifies what it actually wrote, at no re-read cost."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:377
msgid "Write reprenable — `Content-Range` (in-session) **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "Resumable write — `Content-Range` (in-session) **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:379
msgid ""
"Le `PUT` accepte un header optionnel pour reprendre après une coupure "
"réseau sans retransférer tout le binaire :"
msgstr ""
"The `PUT` accepts an optional header to resume after a network drop "
"without retransferring the whole binary:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:386
msgid "Protocole :"
msgstr "Protocol:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:398
msgid ""
"Le device garde la session d'écriture ouverte (handle OTA + état SHA-256)"
" **entre les requêtes** : une déconnexion TCP n'avorte rien. Le Core "
"**chunke** l'image en plusieurs plages et, sur échec, reprend à l'offset "
"rapporté par le device."
msgstr ""
"The device keeps the write session open (OTA handle + SHA-256 state) "
"**between requests**: a TCP disconnect aborts nothing. The Core "
"**chunks** the image into several ranges and, on failure, resumes at "
"the offset reported by the device."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:402
msgid "Réponse de resynchronisation (offset demandé ≠ offset réel) :"
msgstr "Resync response (requested offset ≠ actual offset):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:409
msgid "Réponse de plage intermédiaire :"
msgstr "Intermediate-range response:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:416
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`Content-Range` malformé → `400 {\"error\":\"bad_content_range\"}`."
msgstr "Malformed `Content-Range` → `400 {\"error\":\"bad_content_range\"}`."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:418
msgid ""
"**Reprise inter-reboot** (le device redémarre au milieu du transfert) "
"reste **[RÉSERVE]** : l'état SHA et le handle OTA sont en RAM. Le Core "
"repart alors de `start=0`. La reprise in-session couvre le cas courant "
"(coupure wifi)."
msgstr ""
"**Inter-reboot resumption** (the device reboots mid-transfer) remains "
"**[RESERVED]**: the SHA state and OTA handle live in RAM. The Core then"
" starts over from `start=0`. In-session resumption covers the common "
"case (Wi-Fi drop)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:422
msgid "`POST /v1alpha1/ota/activate`"
msgstr "`POST /v1alpha1/ota/activate`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:424
msgid ""
"L'ESP configure le prochain boot (`esp_ota_set_boot_partition`) et "
"redémarre."
msgstr ""
"The ESP configures the next boot (`esp_ota_set_boot_partition`) and "
"reboots."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:430 ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:610
msgid "Réponse avant reboot :"
msgstr "Response before reboot:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:436
msgid "`GET /v1alpha1/config`"
msgstr "`GET /v1alpha1/config`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:438
msgid ""
"Lit l'état de la configuration de l'agent : valeurs actives (chargées au "
"dernier boot) et valeurs NVS courantes (peut diverger si un `POST "
"/config` a été fait sans reboot depuis)."
msgstr ""
"Reads the agent's configuration state: active values (loaded at the "
"last boot) and current NVS values (may diverge if a `POST /config` was"
" made without a reboot since)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:457
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`generation > active_generation` → config poussée mais reboot en attente."
" Quand NVS est vide (aucun push depuis le flash) : `\"nvs\": {}`, les "
"deux générations valent `0`."
msgstr ""
"`generation > active_generation` → config pushed but reboot pending. "
"When NVS is empty (no push since flashing): `\"nvs\": {}`, both "
"generations are `0`."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:461
msgid "`POST /v1alpha1/config`"
msgstr "`POST /v1alpha1/config`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:463
msgid ""
"Pousse un jeu de clés/valeurs vers le NVS de l'agent. Sémantique **merge-"
"on-key** : seules les clés citées sont écrites, les autres sont "
"inchangées. Les valeurs sont des **chaînes UTF-8** ; l'app interprète le "
"type (`atoi`, `strtof`, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Pushes a set of key/value pairs to the agent's NVS. **Merge-on-key** "
"semantics: only the cited keys are written, the rest are unchanged. "
"Values are **UTF-8 strings**; the app interprets the type (`atoi`, "
"`strtof`, etc.)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:487
msgid ""
"`generation` est incrémenté à chaque `POST /config`. Pour "
"**réinitialiser** une clé au défaut build, pousser la valeur `\"\"` "
"(chaîne vide) — l'agent efface la clé NVS."
msgstr ""
"`generation` is incremented on every `POST /config`. To **reset** a key"
" to its build default, push the value `\"\"` (empty string) — the "
"agent erases the NVS key."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:491
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Restriction (NORMATIF).** La chaîne vide est **réservée** comme "
"sentinelle de reset : elle ne peut pas être stockée comme valeur légitime"
" d'une clé. Une app qui a besoin de distinguer « clé absente » de « clé "
"présente mais sémantiquement vide » (préfixe optionnel, suffixe de "
"topic…) doit encoder ce cas par une sentinelle applicative (ex. une "
"valeur dédiée hors alphabet attendu), pas par `\"\"`. `DELETE "
"/config/{key}` — qui lèverait cette restriction — reste **[RÉSERVE]** "
"(Annexe)."
msgstr ""
"**Restriction (NORMATIVE).** The empty string is **reserved** as the "
"reset sentinel: it cannot be stored as a legitimate value for a key. An"
" app that needs to distinguish \"key absent\" from \"key present but "
"semantically empty\" (optional prefix, topic suffix…) must encode that "
"case with an application-level sentinel (e.g. a dedicated value outside"
" the expected alphabet), not `\"\"`. `DELETE /config/{key}` — which "
"would lift this restriction — remains **[RESERVED]** (Appendix)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:499
msgid "`POST /v1alpha1/app/port`"
msgstr "`POST /v1alpha1/app/port`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:501
msgid ""
"Reconfigure le port TCP du service applicatif embarqué (ex. serveur REST "
"de l'application métier). Pris en compte au prochain démarrage de l'app "
"service."
msgstr ""
"Reconfigures the TCP port of the embedded application service (e.g. the"
" business app's REST server). Takes effect at the next app-service "
"start."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:514
msgid ""
"Contrainte : `1024 ≤ port ≤ 65535`. Valeur persistée en NVS, active au "
"reboot."
msgstr ""
"Constraint: `1024 ≤ port ≤ 65535`. Value persisted in NVS, active on "
"reboot."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:516
msgid "`POST /v1alpha1/tls/cert`"
msgstr "`POST /v1alpha1/tls/cert`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:518
msgid ""
"Pousse un certificat TLS et sa clé privée PEM pour le serveur HTTPS de "
"l'agent. Permet la rotation de certificat sans cycle OTA. Effectif au "
"prochain `embewi_http_start()` (i.e. après reboot)."
msgstr ""
"Pushes a TLS certificate and its private key (PEM) for the agent's "
"HTTPS server. Enables certificate rotation without an OTA cycle. "
"Effective at the next `embewi_http_start()` (i.e. after a reboot)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:535
msgid ""
"Fallback : si aucun certificat n'a été poussé, l'agent utilise un "
"certificat auto-signé EC P-256 généré au build (non secret, pour "
"démarrage sans provisioning TLS préalable)."
msgstr ""
"Fallback: if no certificate has been pushed, the agent uses a "
"self-signed EC P-256 certificate generated at build time (not secret, "
"to allow startup without prior TLS provisioning)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:539
msgid "`POST /v1alpha1/token`"
msgstr "`POST /v1alpha1/token`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:541
msgid ""
"Rotation du token Bearer par node **sans repasser par le portail captif**"
" (qui exige un accès physique). Authentifié avec le token **courant** ; "
"en cas de succès, le nouveau token remplace l'ancien en NVS et devient "
"seul valide."
msgstr ""
"Rotates the per-node Bearer token **without going back through the "
"captive portal** (which requires physical access). Authenticated with "
"the **current** token; on success, the new token replaces the old one "
"in NVS and becomes the only valid one."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:555
msgid "Protocole de rotation sans coupure (responsabilité Core) :"
msgstr "Zero-downtime rotation protocol (Core's responsibility):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:565
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Contrainte : `8 ≤ len(token) ≤ 64`. Atomicité : l'écriture NVS est "
"commitée **avant** la réponse ; si le commit échoue, l'ancien token reste"
" actif et la réponse est `500` (`{\"error\":\"nvs_write_failed\"}`) — pas"
" de fenêtre où aucun token n'est valide. Un token vide (`\"\"`) est "
"**refusé** (`400`) : on ne désactive pas l'auth par rotation (utiliser le"
" portail pour un reset complet)."
msgstr ""
"Constraint: `8 ≤ len(token) ≤ 64`. Atomicity: the NVS write is committed"
" **before** the response; if the commit fails, the old token stays "
"active and the response is `500` (`{\"error\":\"nvs_write_failed\"}`) —"
" no window where no token is valid. An empty token (`\"\"`) is "
"**rejected** (`400`): auth cannot be disabled via rotation (use the "
"portal for a full reset)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:571
msgid ""
"**Rétention côté Core pendant la fenêtre de rotation (NORMATIF).** La "
"mitigation « le Core ré-applique la rotation si le heartbeat reste "
"authentifié à l'ancien token » ne fonctionne que si le Core **peut encore"
" authentifier** ce heartbeat — donc s'il conserve l'ancien token quelque "
"part. Le Core **DOIT** donc retenir `McuSecret.previousToken` tant que "
"l'étape 3 n'est pas confirmée :"
msgstr ""
"**Core-side retention during the rotation window (NORMATIVE).** The "
"mitigation \"the Core re-applies the rotation as long as the heartbeat "
"still authenticates with the old token\" only works if the Core **can "
"still authenticate** that heartbeat — meaning it keeps the old token "
"somewhere. The Core **MUST** therefore retain `McuSecret.previousToken`"
" until step 3 is confirmed:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:588
msgid ""
"Cas explicitement couvert — **crash du Core entre l'étape 1 et l'étape "
"2** : au redémarrage, `McuSecret` contient déjà `token=newToken` **et** "
"`previousToken=oldToken`. Le Core peut ré-émettre l'étape 2 avec "
"`previousToken`, sans reprovisioning physique. Sans cette rétention, le "
"device — qui n'a jamais reçu `newToken` — devient définitivement "
"injoignable en inbound (seul recours : portail captif, accès physique)."
msgstr ""
"Explicitly covered case — **Core crash between step 1 and step 2**: on "
"restart, `McuSecret` already holds both `token=newToken` **and** "
"`previousToken=oldToken`. The Core can re-issue step 2 with "
"`previousToken`, no physical reprovisioning needed. Without this "
"retention, the device — which never received `newToken` — becomes "
"permanently unreachable inbound (only recourse: captive portal, "
"physical access)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:595
msgid ""
"Un heartbeat authentifié avec `previousToken` reste **ACCEPTÉ** pendant "
"cette fenêtre : ce n'est pas une anomalie, c'est le signal attendu tant "
"que l'étape 3 n'a pas convergé."
msgstr ""
"A heartbeat authenticated with `previousToken` remains **ACCEPTED** "
"during this window: this is not an anomaly, it's the expected signal "
"until step 3 has converged."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:599
msgid "`POST /v1alpha1/reboot`"
msgstr "`POST /v1alpha1/reboot`"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:601
msgid ""
"Déclenche un reboot contrôlé, authentifié comme tous les endpoints "
"inbound. Le Core l'utilise pour appliquer un `POST /config` sans cycle "
"OTA complet. Si un OTA est planifié dans la même réconciliation, **ne pas"
" appeler `/reboot` séparément** : `POST /ota/activate` couvre déjà le "
"reboot."
msgstr ""
"Triggers a controlled reboot, authenticated like all inbound endpoints."
" The Core uses it to apply a `POST /config` without a full OTA cycle. "
"If an OTA is scheduled in the same reconcile, **do not call `/reboot` "
"separately**: `POST /ota/activate` already covers the reboot."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:618
msgid "4a. Modèle de config en couches **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "4a. Layered configuration model **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:626
msgid ""
"L'agent lit la config NVS **une seule fois au boot** (`embewi_app_init`)."
" Toute modification nécessite un reboot pour prendre effet — explicite "
"via `POST /reboot` ou implicite via `POST /ota/activate`."
msgstr ""
"The agent reads the NVS config **once at boot** (`embewi_app_init`). "
"Any change requires a reboot to take effect — explicit via `POST "
"/reboot` or implicit via `POST /ota/activate`."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:630
msgid ""
"**L'agent ne valide pas la sémantique des valeurs.** Il stocke et expose."
" La validation (plage GPIO valide, fréquence cohérente…) est "
"responsabilité du Core au moment du push (cf. §9). Mécanisme recommandé :"
" un ValidatingAdmissionWebhook côté Core — voir `embewi-core-design.md` "
"§2 (inclut les limites de taille clé/valeur à faire respecter, couplées "
"aux buffers agent)."
msgstr ""
"**The agent does not validate value semantics.** It stores and exposes."
" Validation (valid GPIO range, consistent frequency…) is the Core's "
"responsibility at push time (see §9). Recommended mechanism: a "
"ValidatingAdmissionWebhook Core-side — see `embewi-core-design.md` §2 "
"(includes the key/value size limits to enforce, tied to the agent's "
"buffers)."

