msgid ""
"`temp_celsius` : capteur interne du SoC, **°C**. Sentinelle **`-127.0`** "
"si le capteur est indisponible (le Core doit filtrer cette valeur)."
msgstr ""
"`temp_celsius`: internal SoC sensor, **°C**. Sentinel value "
"**`-127.0`** if the sensor is unavailable (the Core must filter this "
"value out)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:796
msgid ""
"`task_hwm_min` : plus petit high-water-mark de stack restant, en "
"**octets** (plus c'est proche de 0, plus une task approche de "
"l'overflow). Min sur toutes les tasks si "
"`CONFIG_FREERTOS_USE_TRACE_FACILITY` est actif, sinon HWM de la task "
"heartbeat."
msgstr ""
"`task_hwm_min`: smallest remaining stack high-water-mark, in **bytes** "
"(the closer to 0, the closer a task is to overflow). Minimum across all"
" tasks if `CONFIG_FREERTOS_USE_TRACE_FACILITY` is enabled, otherwise "
"the heartbeat task's HWM."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:800
msgid ""
"`flash_wear_pct` reste **réservé** : pas d'API ESP-IDF pour lire l'usure "
"des partitions OTA/app. Le nom est figé pour le jour où une mesure "
"existera."
msgstr ""
"`flash_wear_pct` remains **reserved**: there is no ESP-IDF API to read "
"OTA/app partition wear. The name is frozen for the day a measurement "
"becomes available."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:803
msgid "Logs"
msgstr "Logs"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:805
msgid "Une ligne JSON par message :"
msgstr "One JSON line per message:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:817
msgid "Flux MVP : `ESP → HTTPS POST → Core /v1alpha1/logs`."
msgstr "MVP flow: `ESP → HTTPS POST → Core /v1alpha1/logs`."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:819
msgid ""
"Transport : le scheme est forcé en `https://` côté agent quel que soit le"
" scheme provisionné en NVS — un `ctrl_url` en `http://` est une erreur de"
" configuration, non une option. Même politique que le heartbeat."
msgstr ""
"Transport: the scheme is forced to `https://` agent-side regardless of "
"the scheme provisioned in NVS — a `ctrl_url` in `http://` is a "
"configuration error, not a fallback option. Same policy as the "
"heartbeat."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:823
msgid "Streaming de logs (WebSocket — outbound) **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "Log streaming (WebSocket — outbound) **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:825
msgid ""
"L'agent ouvre une connexion WebSocket **cliente** vers "
"`wss://ctrl_url_host:port/v1alpha1/logs` — le scheme est toujours "
"`wss://` (contrat §1 : transport chiffré obligatoire), quel que soit le "
"scheme de `ctrl_url`. Tous les messages `ESP_LOGx` — composants IDF, "
"WiFi, OTA, code applicatif, bibliothèques tierces — sont capturés via "
"`esp_log_set_vprintf` et streamés en temps réel sans modification des "
"appels existants."
msgstr ""
"The agent opens a **client** WebSocket connection to "
"`wss://ctrl_url_host:port/v1alpha1/logs` — the scheme is always "
"`wss://` (contract §1: encrypted transport mandatory), regardless of "
"the `ctrl_url` scheme. Every `ESP_LOGx` message — IDF components, WiFi,"
" OTA, application code, third-party libraries — is captured via "
"`esp_log_set_vprintf` and streamed in real time with no changes to "
"existing call sites."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:831
msgid ""
"Format par frame WebSocket (JSON, `level=\"raw\"` — parsing du préfixe "
"IDF hors MVP) :"
msgstr ""
"Format per WebSocket frame (JSON, `level=\"raw\"` — parsing the IDF "
"prefix is out of MVP scope):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:844
msgid ""
"Garantie de livraison : **best-effort, sans buffering inter-"
"reconnexion**. Un ring buffer 4 KB (~25 lignes) absorbe les rafales tant "
"que le WS est connecté. Si le buffer sature alors que le WS est connecté,"
" les nouveaux messages sont silencieusement abandonnés — **on préfère "
"perdre des logs plutôt que bloquer le système**."
msgstr ""
"Delivery guarantee: **best-effort, no buffering across reconnects**. A "
"4 KB ring buffer (~25 lines) absorbs bursts while the WS is connected. "
"If the buffer saturates while the WS is connected, new messages are "
"silently dropped — **we'd rather lose logs than block the system**."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:850
msgid ""
"En cas de **déconnexion WS**, les messages émis pendant la coupure sont "
"**perdus** (la tâche de drain continue de vider le buffer et les jette). "
"Choix assumé pour l'observabilité : à la reconnexion, on diffuse les logs"
" **récents** plutôt qu'un vieux backlog accumulé. Les logs critiques "
"OTA/lifecycle passent de toute façon par `embewi_log_emit()` (HTTP POST, "
"§5 « Logs »), pas par ce canal."
msgstr ""
"On a **WS disconnect**, messages emitted during the outage are "
"**lost** (the drain task keeps emptying the buffer and discarding "
"them). A deliberate observability trade-off: on reconnect, we stream "
"**recent** logs rather than an accumulated old backlog. Critical "
"OTA/lifecycle logs go through `embewi_log_emit()` anyway (HTTP POST, §5"
" \"Logs\"), not through this channel."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:856
msgid ""
"Connexion **device-initiated** (outbound, compatible NAT). Complémentaire"
" à `embewi_log_emit()` qui reste utilisé pour les événements "
"OTA/lifecycle via HTTP POST (envoi immédiat critique)."
msgstr ""
"**Device-initiated** connection (outbound, NAT-compatible). "
"Complementary to `embewi_log_emit()`, still used for OTA/lifecycle "
"events via HTTP POST (critical immediate delivery)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:862
msgid "6. Idempotence et reprise **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "6. Idempotence and resumption **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:864
msgid ""
"Le reconcile du Core **doit** être reprenable. Scénario garanti : le Core"
" crashe entre `/ota/write` et `/ota/activate`."
msgstr ""
"The Core's reconcile **must** be resumable. Guaranteed scenario: the "
"Core crashes between `/ota/write` and `/ota/activate`."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:879
msgid ""
"Sans le champ `staged`, le Core re-transfère 1 MB inutilement à chaque "
"reprise."
msgstr ""
"Without the `staged` field, the Core needlessly re-transfers 1 MB on "
"every resumption."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:881
msgid "**Idempotence config :**"
msgstr "**Config idempotence:**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:896
msgid ""
"Config et OTA peuvent coexister dans la même réconciliation. Ordre "
"canonique : **POST /config d'abord, OTA ensuite** — un seul reboot couvre"
" les deux."
msgstr ""
"Config and OTA can coexist within the same reconcile. Canonical order: "
"**POST /config first, OTA next** — a single reboot covers both."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:901
msgid "7. Politique de binding **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "7. Binding policy **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:903
msgid ""
"Un `McuDeployment` est lié à un **device physique** (le `wheel-"
"controller` est câblé à un moteur précis). Le placement n'est pas du "
"scheduling fongible : c'est une **résolution d'affinité matérielle**."
msgstr ""
"A `McuDeployment` is bound to a **physical device** (the "
"`wheel-controller` is wired to one specific motor). Placement is not "
"fungible scheduling: it's **hardware-affinity resolution**."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:914
msgid "On privilégie le pin explicite :"
msgstr "Explicit pinning is preferred:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:921
msgid "plutôt que le sélecteur qui peut matcher plusieurs devices :"
msgstr "over a selector that may match several devices:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:929
msgid ""
"Conflit (deux McuDeployment visant le même ESP) : **first-bound wins**, "
"le second part en erreur `DeviceBusy`. Pas de préemption en MVP."
msgstr ""
"Conflict (two McuDeployments targeting the same ESP): **first-bound "
"wins**, the second one fails with `DeviceBusy`. No preemption in the "
"MVP."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:932
msgid ""
"**Orchestration de flotte.** La mise à jour coordonnée de N devices "
"identiques (rolling/canary, rollback sur taux d'échec) est portée par un "
"`McuDeploymentSet` **purement côté Core** — voir `embewi-core-design.md` "
"§1. Cet objet génère des `McuDeployment` unitaires et n'ajoute aucune "
"surface côté agent."
msgstr ""
"**Fleet orchestration.** Coordinated rollout across N identical devices"
" (rolling/canary, rollback on failure rate) is carried by a "
"`McuDeploymentSet` **purely Core-side** — see `embewi-core-design.md` "
"§1. This object generates unit `McuDeployment`s and adds no agent-side "
"surface."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:940
msgid "7a. McuConfigMap **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "7a. McuConfigMap **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:942
msgid ""
"Ressource Kubernetes portée par le Core, indépendante du binaire. "
"Découple le câblage matériel (GPIOs, fréquences, adresses I²C…) de "
"l'image OTA."
msgstr ""
"Kubernetes resource carried by the Core, independent from the binary. "
"Decouples hardware wiring (GPIOs, frequencies, I²C addresses…) from the"
" OTA image."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:956
msgid "Référence depuis un `McuDeployment` (optionnel — absent = défauts build) :"
msgstr "Referenced from a `McuDeployment` (optional — absent = build defaults):"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:967
msgid "**Règles de binding McuConfigMap → device :**"
msgstr "**McuConfigMap → device binding rules:**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:975
msgid ""
"Un `McuConfigMap` peut être partagé entre plusieurs `McuDeployment` "
"ciblant des devices **identiquement câblés**. La modification du "
"`McuConfigMap` déclenche une réconciliation sur tous les devices qui y "
"référencent."
msgstr ""
"A `McuConfigMap` can be shared across several `McuDeployment`s targeting"
" **identically wired** devices. Modifying the `McuConfigMap` triggers a"
" reconcile on every device referencing it."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:981
msgid "8. Effets Kubernetes **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "8. Kubernetes effects **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:983
msgid ""
"Service **selectorless** + EndpointSlice géré à la main par le "
"contrôleur. L'endpoint pointe **directement sur l'IP de management de "
"l'ESP** (pas de Pod IP logique en MVP — elle reviendrait seulement avec "
"un vrai proxy/NAT)."
msgstr ""
"**Selectorless** Service + EndpointSlice managed by hand by the "
"controller. The endpoint points **directly at the ESP's management "
"IP** (no logical Pod IP in the MVP — that would only come back with a "
"real proxy/NAT)."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:996
msgid ""
"**IP de l'endpoint (NORMATIF).** Le Core **DOIT** mettre à jour "
"`endpoints[].addresses` avec le champ `ip` du heartbeat à chaque "
"réception. L'IP source TCP n'est pas utilisée : elle peut différer de "
"l'IP de management en présence d'un proxy ou d'un routage asymétrique."
msgstr ""
"**Endpoint IP (NORMATIVE).** The Core **MUST** update "
"`endpoints[].addresses` with the heartbeat's `ip` field on every "
"reception. The TCP source IP is not used: it can differ from the "
"management IP in the presence of a proxy or asymmetric routing."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1006
msgid ""
"Cette règle rend l'IP dynamique (DHCP) transparente : le prochain "
"heartbeat (toutes les 5 s) suffit à corriger le routage après un "
"changement d'adresse, sans re-provisioning. Un device avec IP statique "
"NVS converge immédiatement."
msgstr ""
"This rule makes a dynamic IP (DHCP) transparent: the next heartbeat "
"(every 5 s) is enough to fix routing after an address change, with no "
"re-provisioning. A device with a static NVS IP converges immediately."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1010
msgid "Pilotage de `ready` :"
msgstr "Driving `ready`:"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1019
msgid ""
"Le Core **ne marque jamais** un déploiement `Ready` avant la confirmation"
" agent (`state=running` + `ota_validated=true` + bon `deployment_id`). Le"
" healthcheck devient routage, gratuitement."
msgstr ""
"The Core **never marks** a deployment `Ready` before agent confirmation"
" (`state=running` + `ota_validated=true` + matching `deployment_id`). "
"Healthchecking becomes routing, for free."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1023
msgid ""
"**Détection de divergence `heartbeat.ip` (NORMATIF).** Le Core compare "
"`heartbeat.ip` à l'IP source TCP de la requête. En cas de divergence, il "
"émet l'Event Kubernetes `HeartbeatIPMismatch` (Warning) — sans rejeter le"
" heartbeat ni bloquer la mise à jour de l'`EndpointSlice` : un proxy ou "
"un routage asymétrique légitime peut produire cette divergence (cf. §1, "
"rayon d'action d'un token compromis). C'est une détection, pas un "
"blocage."
msgstr ""
"**`heartbeat.ip` divergence detection (NORMATIVE).** The Core compares "
"`heartbeat.ip` to the request's TCP source IP. On divergence, it emits "
"the Kubernetes Event `HeartbeatIPMismatch` (Warning) — without "
"rejecting the heartbeat or blocking the `EndpointSlice` update: a "
"legitimate proxy or asymmetric routing can produce this divergence (see"
" §1, blast radius of a compromised token). This is detection, not "
"blocking."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1030
msgid ""
"Restriction CIDR de `heartbeat.ip` (optionnelle, **hors MVP**) : borner "
"`heartbeat.ip` au CIDR de management (même clé `allowed_cidr` que §1) et "
"rejeter (`400`) un heartbeat hors CIDR bornerait la redirection au subnet"
" isolé. Non retenue pour le MVP — à activer si le risque de redirection "
"de trafic est jugé prioritaire pour un déploiement donné."
msgstr ""
"CIDR restriction on `heartbeat.ip` (optional, **out of MVP**): bounding "
"`heartbeat.ip` to the management CIDR (same `allowed_cidr` key as §1) "
"and rejecting (`400`) a heartbeat outside that CIDR would confine "
"traffic redirection to the isolated subnet. Not adopted for the MVP — "
"to enable if traffic-redirection risk is judged a priority for a given "
"deployment."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1036
msgid ""
"**Sécurité réseau (défense en profondeur).** Le subnet de management des "
"ESP doit être isolé sur un VLAN dédié et protégé par une NetworkPolicy "
"K8s (egress vers le subnet ESP réservé aux Pods Core). Côté agent, "
"`CONFIG_EMBEWI_ENABLE_IP_FILTER` (opt-in production) rejette les "
"connexions hors du CIDR autorisé avant tout handler, via `open_fn` du "
"serveur HTTPS. Le CIDR est configurable par McuConfigMap (`allowed_cidr` "
"— cluster CIDR recommandé). Ces trois couches (VLAN + NetworkPolicy + "
"filtrage agent) sont complémentaires au token Bearer."
msgstr ""
"**Network security (defense in depth).** The ESP management subnet "
"should be isolated on a dedicated VLAN and protected by a K8s "
"NetworkPolicy (egress to the ESP subnet restricted to Core Pods). "
"Agent-side, `CONFIG_EMBEWI_ENABLE_IP_FILTER` (production opt-in) rejects"
" connections outside the allowed CIDR before any handler, via the "
"HTTPS server's `open_fn`. The CIDR is configurable via McuConfigMap "
"(`allowed_cidr` — cluster CIDR recommended). These three layers (VLAN +"
" NetworkPolicy + agent filtering) complement the Bearer token."

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1047
msgid "8a. Status conditions des CRDs **[NORMATIF]**"
msgstr "8a. CRD status conditions **[NORMATIVE]**"

#: ../../embewi-contract-v2.md:1049
msgid ""
"Les CRDs exposent des `.status.conditions[]` au format Kubernetes "
"standard (`type` / `status` / `reason` / `message` / "
"`lastTransitionTime`). Cela permet l'intégration native avec `kubectl "
"wait`, ArgoCD, Flux et tout outillage K8s qui observe les conditions."
msgstr ""
"CRDs expose `.status.conditions[]` in the standard Kubernetes format "
"(`type` / `status` / `reason` / `message` / `lastTransitionTime`). This"
" enables native integration with `kubectl wait`, ArgoCD, Flux, and any "
"K8s tooling that watches conditions."

